{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And the meaning of \"far off is what was\":</b> For what was is far off by itself, and a thing that has not yet come to pass — a person could search until he finds it. And this is a deep matter, deep: who can find it? Like the matter of \"deep waters, counsel in a person's heart\" (Proverbs 20:5) — and a person of understanding draws it out."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The verse citations in the commentary are implicit; Proverbs 20:5 is resolved from the quoted phrase 'מים עמוקים עצה בלב איש ואיש תבונות ידלנה.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:14.553279578Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}